    "id": "creative-direction",
    "description": "Art direction in one pass — intent, palette, fonts, beat-to-preset map, layout strategy. Load once per new full-path cut.",
    "content": "---\nname: creative-direction\ndescription: Art direction in one pass — intent, palette, fonts, beat-to-preset map, layout strategy. Load once per new full-path cut.\n---\n\n# Creative direction\n\nOne call, five decisions. Everything downstream (plan, presets, layout, skills) reads off this.\n\n## 1. Intent (one sentence)\n\nWhat the cut must ACHIEVE, not what it shows. \"Make a $49 course feel like a $499 transformation in 5 seconds\" beats \"text animation with logo\". If you can't name the job, you can't direct the cut.\n\n## 2. Palette (three hues max)\n\nBackground + ink + ONE accent. Restraint reads premium; every extra hue halves the impact.\n\n| Mood | bg | ink | accent |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| cinematic (default) | #0B0C10 | #F2F3F7 | #FFB340 |\n| energetic | #101014 | #F4F2EC | #FF5A5A |\n| playful | #1B1035 | #F4F2EC | #FF7AD9 |\n| minimal | #F4F2EC | #141414 | #E4572E |\n| elegant | #111214 | #EFE9DC | #D8B56B |\n| tech | #0B0E14 | #E8EEF7 | #5AC8FA |\n\nDark stages forgive; light stages expose. Minimal gets ONE accent and no glow.\n\n## 3. Font pair (voice, not decoration)\n\nOne display + one text (see `typography` pairings). The pairing IS the brand voice: Unbounded+Manrope (modern), Anton+Archivo (bold), Instrument Serif+Newsreader (elegant), Space Grotesk+Space Mono (tech).\n\n## 4. Beat→preset map (motion with intent)\n\nEvery beat gets a preset id AND a reason: anticipation (weight), entrance (arrival), cascade (readability), counter-motion (depth), settle (landing), hold (resolve). A beat without a motion reason is decoration — cut it or justify it.\n\n## 5. Layout strategy (see `layout-composition`)\n\ncenter-stack (default hero), split-rail (text left, emblem right), mask (kinetic type), terminal (code), lower-third (broadcast). Pick from the BRIEF shape: code-ish → terminal, speaker → lower-third, short punchy → mask, everything else → stack/split by seed.\n\n## Taste rules (non-negotiable)\n\n- Restraint reads premium: one accent, one display face, one idea per beat.\n- Motion earns attention: anticipation → overshoot → settle → breathing hold. A still frame with nice type is a poster, not a cut.\n- Staging (Disney): the presentation of an idea so it is COMPLETELY and unmistakably clear. One focal element per beat; everything else supports or leaves.\n- Exaggerate, then pull back 10%: sadder, bolder, snappier. Timid reads as broken.\n"
